# LEGAL TAX - EXAM QUICK REFERENCE GUIDE
## Income Tax Act, 1961 - Complete Study Material

---

# SECTION 1: BASICS OF INCOME TAX

## Section 2(24) - Definition of Income
- **Definition**: INCLUSIVE (not exhaustive) - covers items mentioned + any receipt having nature of income
- **Income Includes**:
  - Profits & gains from business/profession
  - Dividend income
  - Voluntary contributions to charitable trusts
  - Perquisites & profits in lieu of salary
  - Capital gains from transfer of capital assets
  - Winnings from lotteries, gambling, betting (special rates)
  - Life insurance proceeds (except exempt under Sec 10(10D))
  - Deemed incomes (gifts beyond limits)

---

## STEPS TO DETERMINE TAXABLE INCOME

### Step I: Determine Nature of Receipt
| Type | Examples | Taxability |
|------|----------|------------|
| **Income Receipt** | Salary, Business income, Rent, Interest | Generally Taxable |
| **Capital Receipt** | Sale of assets, Loans, Gifts | Generally NOT taxable (exceptions exist) |

### Taxability of Gifts
- **Taxable if**: Aggregate value > Rs.50,000/year from non-relatives
- **EXEMPT Gifts**:
  - From relatives (as defined under IT Act)
  - On occasion of marriage
  - From local authorities
  - From approved charitable/religious trusts
  - From educational institutions

### Step II: Taxable Capital Receipts
1. **Capital Gains** - profit from transfer of capital assets
2. **Taxable Gifts** - >Rs.50,000 from non-relatives
3. **Compensation on compulsory acquisition**
4. **Share premium in excess of FMV**
5. **Forfeiture of advance money**
6. **Deemed capital receipts**

### Step III: Tax Exempt Income (Section 10)

| Section | Income Type | Exemption |
|---------|-------------|-----------|
| **10(1)** | Agricultural Income | Fully Exempt |
| **10(2A)** | Partner's share of profit | Exempt (firm already taxed) |
| **10(20)** | Local Authorities Income | Fully Exempt |
| **Sec 11** | Charitable/Religious Trust | Exempt if used for approved purposes |
| **10(16)** | Scholarships | Fully Exempt |
| **10(10)** | Gratuity | Exempt up to limits |
| **10(5)** | LTA | Exempt for domestic travel |
| **10(13A)** | HRA | Partially Exempt |

---

## FIVE HEADS OF INCOME (Section 14)

| Head | Sections | Key Components |
|------|----------|----------------|
| **1. Income from Salary** | 15-17 | Basic salary, Allowances, Bonus, Perquisites |
| **2. House Property** | 22-27 | NAV - Municipal Tax - 30% SD - Interest on loan |
| **3. Business/Profession** | 28-44DB | Business income minus allowable expenses |
| **4. Capital Gains** | 45-55A | STCG & LTCG from asset transfer |
| **5. Other Sources** | 56-59 | Interest, Dividend, Gifts, Residual income |

---

## COMPUTING TOTAL INCOME

**Formula:**
```
Gross Total Income (GTI) = Sum of all 5 heads
Total Income = GTI - Chapter VI-A Deductions (80C to 80U)
```

---

# SECTION 2: CHAPTER VI-A DEDUCTIONS

| Section | Deduction For | Limit |
|---------|---------------|-------|
| **80C** | PPF, ELSS, LIC, etc. | Max Rs.1,50,000 |
| **80D** | Medical Insurance Premium | Varies by age |
| **80E** | Interest on Education Loan | Full interest |
| **80G** | Donations to approved institutions | 50% or 100% (with/without 10% limit) |
| **80TTA** | Savings Bank Interest | Up to Rs.10,000 |
| **80TTB** | Interest for Senior Citizens | Up to Rs.50,000 |
| **80CCD(2)** | Employer's NPS Contribution | Up to 10% of salary |

---

# SECTION 3: TAX REGIMES (FY 2023-24)

## OLD TAX REGIME
| Income Range | Tax Rate |
|--------------|----------|
| Up to Rs.2,50,000 | NIL |
| Rs.2,50,001 - Rs.5,00,000 | 5% |
| Rs.5,00,001 - Rs.10,00,000 | 20% |
| Above Rs.10,00,000 | 30% |

**Features**: Allows all exemptions & deductions

## NEW TAX REGIME (Section 115BAC) - DEFAULT
| Income Range | Tax Rate |
|--------------|----------|
| Up to Rs.3,00,000 | NIL |
| Rs.3,00,001 - Rs.6,00,000 | 5% |
| Rs.6,00,001 - Rs.9,00,000 | 10% |
| Rs.9,00,001 - Rs.12,00,000 | 15% |
| Rs.12,00,001 - Rs.15,00,000 | 20% |
| Above Rs.15,00,000 | 30% |

**Features**: Lower rates but MOST deductions NOT allowed
**Allowed**: Standard Deduction (Rs.50,000), Employer NPS (80CCD(2)), Agricultural Income exempt

---

# SECTION 4: WAYS OF PAYING TAX

## I. Advance Tax
- **Who**: Tax liability > Rs.10,000/year
- **Due Dates**:
  - 15th June - 15%
  - 15th September - 45%
  - 15th December - 75%
  - 15th March - 100%

## II. TDS (Tax Deducted at Source)
- Deducted by payer at time of payment
- **Applies to**: Salary, Interest, Rent, Professional fees, Commission

## III. Self-Assessment Tax
- Balance tax after adjusting Advance Tax & TDS
- Paid before filing return

---

# SECTION 5: SURCHARGE & CESS

## Surcharge (on Income Tax)
| Total Income | Surcharge Rate |
|--------------|----------------|
| Up to Rs.50 lakh | NIL |
| Rs.50 lakh - Rs.1 crore | 10% |
| Rs.1 crore - Rs.2 crore | 15% |
| Rs.2 crore - Rs.5 crore | 25% |
| Above Rs.5 crore | 37% |

## Health & Education Cess
- **Rate**: 4% on (Income Tax + Surcharge)

---

# SECTION 6: CONCEALED INCOME (Section 115BBE)

| Section | Type of Concealment |
|---------|---------------------|
| **68** | Unexplained cash credits |
| **69** | Unexplained investments |
| **69A** | Unexplained assets (cash, bullion, jewellery) |
| **69B** | Excess investment over declared |
| **69C** | Unexplained expenditure |

**TAX RATE: FLAT 60%** (+ surcharge & cess)

---

# SECTION 7: RESIDENTIAL STATUS (Section 6)

## Basic Conditions for RESIDENT
Must satisfy ANY ONE:
1. Stay in India >= 182 days in previous year, OR
2. Stay >= 60 days in PY AND >= 365 days in preceding 4 years

## Types of Residents

### A. Resident & Ordinarily Resident (ROR)
- **Additional Conditions** (BOTH required):
  - Resident in at least 2 of 10 preceding years
  - Stay >= 730 days in preceding 7 years
- **Taxability**: Global income taxable

### B. Resident but Not Ordinarily Resident (RNOR)
- **Conditions** (ANY ONE):
  - Non-resident in 9 of 10 preceding years, OR
  - Stay <= 729 days in preceding 7 years
- **Taxability**: Indian income + Business controlled from India

### C. Non-Resident (NR)
- Does NOT satisfy basic conditions
- **Taxability**: Only Indian income taxable

## Bank Accounts for NRIs

| Account | Currency | Repatriation | Interest Tax |
|---------|----------|--------------|--------------|
| **NRO** | INR | Restricted | Taxable + TDS |
| **NRE** | INR | Fully Free | EXEMPT (Sec 10(4)) |
| **FCNR** | Foreign | Fully Free | EXEMPT |
| **RFC** | Foreign | Free | Exempt 2 years (RNOR), then taxable |

---

# SECTION 8: CLUBBING OF INCOME (Section 64)

## Purpose
Prevent tax evasion by transferring income to relatives in lower tax brackets

## Clubbing Provisions

| Section | Situation | Clubbing With |
|---------|-----------|---------------|
| **64(1)(ii)** | Spouse's salary from concern where assessee has substantial interest | Assessee's income |
| **64(1)(iv)** | Income from asset transferred to spouse without adequate consideration | Transferor's income |
| **64(1)(vi)** | Income from asset transferred to son's wife | Transferor's income |
| **64(1A)** | Minor child's income | Parent with higher income |
| **64(1)(v)** | Income from revocable transfer | Transferor's income |

### Exceptions to Clubbing:
- Spouse employed due to professional/technical qualifications
- Transfer under agreement to live apart
- Minor's income from:
  - Manual work
  - Skill/talent/specialized knowledge
  - Disabled child (Sec 80U)

### Minor Child Income
- **Exemption**: Rs.1,500 per child per year
- Remaining clubbed with higher-earning parent

---

# SECTION 9: SECTION 80G - DONATIONS

## Types of Deductions

| Category | Deduction | 10% Limit |
|----------|-----------|-----------|
| **A** | 100% | NO limit (PM Relief Fund, Defence Fund, PM CARES) |
| **B** | 50% | NO limit |
| **C** | 100% or 50% | Subject to 10% of Adjusted Total Income |

## Adjusted Total Income =
Total Income MINUS:
- Deductions 80C to 80U (except 80G)
- Long-term capital gains
- Short-term capital gains u/s 111A
- Income taxed at special rates

---

# SECTION 10: SALARY INCOME

## Section 15 - Chargeability
- Taxable on **DUE or RECEIPT basis** (whichever earlier)
- Includes: Basic, Allowances, Bonus, Commission, Perquisites, Advance salary, Arrears
- **Advance salary**: Taxable in year of receipt
- **Arrears**: Taxable in year of receipt (Relief u/s 89 available)

## Section 16 - Deductions from Salary

| Section | Deduction | Amount |
|---------|-----------|--------|
| **16(1)** | Standard Deduction | Rs.50,000 |
| **16(2)** | Entertainment Allowance | Only Govt employees (Least of: Actual, Rs.5,000, 20% of basic) |
| **16(3)** | Professional Tax | Actual paid (max ~Rs.2,500/year) |

---

# SECTION 11: PERQUISITES (Section 17(2))

## Definition
Any benefit/amenity provided by employer FREE or at concessional rate

## Types of Perquisites

| Type | Section | Taxable Value |
|------|---------|---------------|
| **Rent-Free Accommodation** | 17(2)(i) | Based on employer type, city, salary |
| **Concessional Loans** | 17(2)(vii) | SBI rate - Actual rate charged |
| **Motor Car** | 17(2)(iii) | Depends on purpose & who bears expenses |
| **ESOPs** | 17(2)(vi) | FMV - Exercise Price (at exercise) |
| **Medical Facilities** | 17(2) | Excess over exemption limit |

### Loan Exemptions:
- Loan <= Rs.20,000
- Medical loan for specified diseases (80DDB)

### Motor Car - NOT taxable if:
- Used only for official purpose
- Records maintained

---

# SECTION 12: ALLOWANCES (Section 10)

## I. Leave Travel Allowance - LTA [Sec 10(5)]
- **Exempt**: Domestic travel expenses only
- **Conditions**:
  - 2 journeys in block of 4 years
  - Only transportation (NOT hotel, food, sightseeing)
  - Travel within India
  - Can carry forward 1 unused journey

## II. House Rent Allowance - HRA [Sec 10(13A)]
**Exemption = LEAST of:**
1. Actual HRA received
2. Rent paid - 10% of salary (Basic + DA)
3. 50% of salary (Metro) OR 40% (Non-Metro)

## III. Gratuity [Sec 10(10)]
- **Govt employees**: Fully EXEMPT
- **Others**: Exempt up to Rs.20 LAKH

## IV. Leave Encashment [Sec 10(10AA)]
- **Govt employees**: Fully EXEMPT
- **Others**: Exempt up to Rs.3 LAKH

## V. VRS [Sec 10(10C)]
- **Exempt**: Up to Rs.5 LAKH
- **Conditions**:
  - 10 years service OR 40 years age
  - Exemption only ONCE

---

# SECTION 13: ESOP (Employee Stock Option Plan)

## Key Features
- Right to purchase shares at predetermined price after vesting period
- Lock-in period: Generally 3 years
- Needs shareholder approval

## Taxation - TWO STAGES

### 1. At Exercise (Perquisite Tax)
**Taxable Value = FMV on exercise date - Exercise Price**
- Taxed as Salary Income
- TDS by employer

### 2. At Sale (Capital Gains)
**Capital Gain = Sale Price - Exercise Price**

| Type | Holding Period | Tax Rate |
|------|----------------|----------|
| **STCG** | <= 36 months | 15% |
| **LTCG** | > 36 months | 10% (above Rs.1 lakh) |

---

# SECTION 14: HOUSE PROPERTY (Section 22-24)

## Section 22 - Chargeability
- Income from building/land owned by assessee
- Tax on Annual Value (ownership basis, not receipt)

## Section 24 - Deductions

| Deduction | Section | Amount |
|-----------|---------|--------|
| **Standard Deduction** | 24(a) | 30% of Annual Value |
| **Interest on Home Loan** | 24(b) | Up to Rs.2 lakh (self-occupied) |

## Computation Formula
```
Income from House Property =
Annual Value
- Municipal Taxes Paid
- 30% Standard Deduction
- Interest on Home Loan
```

## Co-Ownership
- Each co-owner taxed separately
- Deductions in proportion to ownership share

---

# SECTION 15: SECTION 72A - CARRY FORWARD (AMALGAMATION/DEMERGER)

## Purpose
Tax relief in corporate restructuring - allows carry forward of losses & unabsorbed depreciation

## Amalgamation (Merger)
**Conditions**:
1. Government approval
2. Transfer ALL assets & liabilities
3. Continue business of transferor
4. Transferee holds >= 75% voting power
5. Business continued for >= 5 years after amalgamation

## Demerger
**Conditions**:
1. Transfer part of business with assets/liabilities
2. Shareholders get shares in resulting company (proportionate)
3. Both companies continue to exist
4. No sale of shares involved
5. Accounting as per Companies Act, 2013

---

# SECTION 16: DEPRECIATION (Section 32)

## Meaning
Reduction in asset value due to wear & tear, usage, obsolescence

## Methods

### I. Straight Line Method (SLM)
- Fixed rate on ORIGINAL COST every year
- **Formula**: Depreciation = Original Cost x Rate

### II. Written Down Value (WDV) - Used under IT Act
- Rate on BOOK VALUE (reducing balance)
- **Formula**: Depreciation = Book Value x Rate

## Depreciation Rates (WDV)
| Asset | Rate |
|-------|------|
| Residential Building | 5% |
| Other Buildings | 10% |
| Plant & Machinery | 15% |
| Intangible Assets | 25% |

## Conditions for Claiming
1. **Ownership** of asset
2. **Eligible assets** (Tangible: Buildings, Plant, Machinery, Furniture; Intangible: Patents, Trademarks, Copyrights, Licenses, Know-how)
3. **Used for business/profession**
4. **Put to use** in that year

**NOTE**: Land is NOT depreciable

---

# SECTION 17: SECTION 37 - GENERAL BUSINESS EXPENSES

## Conditions
- Expense must be WHOLLY and EXCLUSIVELY for business
- NOT covered under Sections 30-36

## Allowed Expenses
- Rent for business premises
- Salaries and wages
- Legal and professional fees
- Office expenses
- Advertising and marketing

## NOT Allowed
- Personal expenses
- Capital expenditure
- Illegal/prohibited activities

---

# SECTION 18: LEASE CONCEPTS

## Parties
- **Lessee**: Rents the asset, pays lease rent (DEDUCTIBLE)
- **Lessor**: Owns asset, receives rent (can claim depreciation)

## Types of Leasing
| Type | Feature | Suitable For |
|------|---------|--------------|
| **Front-End** | Higher payments initially | Strong initial cash flow |
| **Back-End** | Lower payments initially | Growing businesses, startups |
| **Balloon** | Large final payment | Vehicles, heavy machinery |

---

# SECTION 19: MAT & UNABSORBED DEPRECIATION

## MAT (Minimum Alternate Tax) - Section 115JB
- Ensures companies pay minimum tax
- Calculated on BOOK PROFITS (not taxable income)
- Applicable to companies

## Unabsorbed Depreciation
- Depreciation not fully adjusted in a year
- Carry forward: NO TIME LIMIT
- Set off against ANY head (except Salary)

## Business Loss Carry Forward
- Carry forward: 8 assessment years
- Set off: Only against business income
- Return must be filed within due date

---

# SECTION 20: SECTION 35AB - KNOW-HOW EXPENDITURE

## Applicability
Capital expenditure for acquiring:
- Patents
- Technical processes
- Designs
- Technology transfer rights

## Amortization
- **Period**: 6 years
- **Deduction**: 1/6th of total expenditure per year

---

# SECTION 21: DTAA (Double Tax Avoidance Agreement)

## Meaning
Bilateral agreement between countries to prevent same income being taxed twice

## Methods of Relief
1. **Exemption Method** - Tax in only one country
2. **Tax Credit Method** - Credit for foreign tax paid
3. **Deduction Method** - Foreign tax as expense

## Indo-Mauritius DTAA
- **Old benefit**: Capital gains on Indian shares taxable only in Mauritius (effectively tax-free)
- **Amendment**: Now may be taxable in India depending on date of acquisition

## Conditions to Claim DTAA Benefits
1. Permanent place of abode in treaty country
2. Tax residency in DTAA country
3. Centre of vital interests (family, business, employment)

## Permanent Establishment (PE)
- **Definition**: Fixed place of business in another country
- **Examples**: Branch, Factory, Office, Workshop
- **If PE exists**: Income attributable to PE is taxable in source country
- **Communication/Liaison office**: Does NOT create PE

---

# SECTION 22: CAPITAL GAINS (Section 45)

## Section 45 - Chargeability
- Profits from transfer of capital asset = Capital Gains
- Taxable in year of transfer
- For immovable property: Date of registration = Date of transfer

## Capital Gain Formula
```
Capital Gain = Sale Consideration - Cost of Acquisition - Transfer Expenses
```

## Transfer (Section 2(47)) Includes:
- Sale
- Exchange
- Gift
- Relinquishment
- Compulsory acquisition
- Parting with possession
- Distribution on dissolution of partnership
- Extinguishment of rights

## Capital Loss Carry Forward
- Carry forward: 8 assessment years
- Set off: ONLY against capital gains
- Return must be filed on time

---

## STCG vs LTCG

| Asset Type | Short-Term | Long-Term |
|------------|------------|-----------|
| General | < 36 months | >= 36 months |
| Immovable Property | < 24 months | >= 24 months |
| Listed Equity Shares | < 12 months | >= 12 months |

## Tax Rates
| Type | Rate |
|------|------|
| **STCG (Equity with STT)** | 15% |
| **STCG (Others)** | Normal slab rates |
| **LTCG (Equity)** | 10% (above Rs.1 lakh) |
| **LTCG (Others)** | 20% with indexation |

## Section 10(37) - Agricultural Land Exemption
- **Exempt**: Land > 8 km from municipality/city
- **Taxable**: Land within 8 km (urban)

---

## Section 2(14) - Capital Asset

### Includes:
Property of any kind - movable/immovable, tangible/intangible

### EXCLUDES (NOT Capital Assets):
1. Stock-in-trade
2. Personal effects (except jewellery, paintings, sculptures, art)
3. Agricultural land in RURAL India (outside 8 km of municipality with population >= 10,000)
4. Indian currency
5. Gold bonds under Gold Bonds Act, 1965

---

# SECTION 23: TAXATION OF ENTITIES

| Entity | Tax Rate | Notes |
|--------|----------|-------|
| **Individual** | 5% to 30% (slabs) | Basic exemption available |
| **HUF** | Same as Individual | Separate PAN, separate return |
| **Partnership Firm** | 30% FLAT | No basic exemption, partner's share exempt in their hands |
| **Domestic Company** | 25% (turnover <= Rs.400 cr) / 30% | Based on turnover |
| **Foreign Company** | 40% FLAT | On income earned in India |
| **AOP** | Individual slab rates | Separate taxable entity |
| **Charitable Trusts** | May be exempt (Sec 11) | If income used for charitable purposes |

---

# SECTION 24: PRESUMPTIVE TAXATION

## Section 44AD - Small Business
- **Eligibility**: Resident Individual, HUF, Partnership (NOT LLP)
- **Turnover Limit**: Rs.2 crore (Rs.3 crore if cash receipts/payments <= 5%)
- **Presumptive Income**:
  - Cash receipts: 8%
  - Digital receipts: 6%
- **Books/Audit**: NOT required if income >= presumptive rate
- **Opt-out restriction**: Cannot re-enter for 5 years

## Section 44ADA - Professionals
- **Eligibility**: Resident individuals/firms in specified professions
- **Professions**: Legal, Medical, Engineering, Architectural, Accountancy, Technical consultancy, Interior decoration
- **Gross Receipts Limit**: Rs.50 lakh
- **Presumptive Income**: 50% of gross receipts

## Section 44AE - Transport Business
- **Eligibility**: Own <= 10 goods vehicles
- **Presumptive Income**:
  - Heavy Goods Vehicle: Rs.1,000/ton GVW/month
  - Other vehicles: Rs.7,500/vehicle/month

## Other Presumptive Sections (Non-Residents)
| Section | Business | Rate |
|---------|----------|------|
| **44B** | Shipping | 7.5% of gross receipts |
| **44BB** | Oil/Mineral Exploration | 10% of gross receipts |
| **44BBA** | Aircraft Operation | 5% of gross receipts |
| **44BBB** | Power Projects (Foreign Co.) | 10% of gross receipts |
| **44BBC** | Cruise Ships | As notified |

## Common Provisions
- **Advance Tax**: 100% by 15th March (no installments)
- **Chapter VI-A Deductions**: ALLOWED
- **Business Deductions (30-38)**: NOT allowed separately

